00:37:23.650 --> 00:37:26.410
But then the next was
to emphasize this notion

00:37:26.410 --> 00:37:28.730
that the world is
moving very fast.

00:37:28.730 --> 00:37:31.690
And it's not just about how to
provide secure connectivity,

00:37:31.690 --> 00:37:33.760
but how to get into
the fabric of what

00:37:33.760 --> 00:37:35.140
the application is doing.

00:37:35.140 --> 00:37:36.640
And if we don't
understand, we don't

00:37:36.640 --> 00:37:39.550
secure, we don't control
what applications are doing,

00:37:39.550 --> 00:37:41.470
what users are doing
with these applications,

00:37:41.470 --> 00:37:43.690
and what data elements
are being touched, means

00:37:43.690 --> 00:37:45.690
that we don't really have
control and visibility

00:37:45.690 --> 00:37:46.790
of infrastructure.

00:37:46.790 --> 00:37:49.540
And this is the idea that
we have to get into--

00:37:49.540 --> 00:37:52.060
the Service Mesh fabric,
or the business fabric,

00:37:52.060 --> 00:37:54.850
of the communications, that
enable us to essentially now

00:37:54.850 --> 00:37:57.160
take control at the
behavioral level,

00:37:57.160 --> 00:37:58.840
at the SLA level,
at the security

00:37:58.840 --> 00:38:01.330
level, of what applications do.

00:38:01.330 --> 00:38:04.870
And this is essentially what
drove VMware and Google working

00:38:04.870 --> 00:38:05.800
together.

00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:08.050
And as a summary, essentially
we were saying, in order

00:38:08.050 --> 00:38:11.470
to enable our
customers' enterprises

00:38:11.470 --> 00:38:14.350
to essentially achieve a
true hybrid cloud story,

00:38:14.350 --> 00:38:17.890
we started by connectivity
and application level QSS.

00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:20.900
But essentially, we have to
go to service management,

00:38:20.900 --> 00:38:22.150
and understand the end to end.

00:38:22.150 --> 00:38:23.740
Because at the end
