00:38:31.990 --> 00:38:35.180
to become faster, to deliver
new value to their customers.

00:38:35.180 --> 00:38:36.990
And this essentially
has to be done

00:38:36.990 --> 00:38:39.490
while maintaining the enterprise
class capabilities of being

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:42.160
able to operate it with
the security guarantees,

00:38:42.160 --> 00:38:44.170
and the visibility
elements, that

00:38:44.170 --> 00:38:47.350
the operational environments
of enterprises may need.

00:38:47.350 --> 00:38:49.300
So as a summary, I
wanted to emphasize

00:38:49.300 --> 00:38:52.120
what Ines was saying, that
the two companies are working

00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:55.210
together, and very committed
to the open source frameworks

00:38:55.210 --> 00:38:56.380
that we are using.

00:38:56.380 --> 00:38:58.810
We are working a lot
on the public domain,

00:38:58.810 --> 00:39:01.930
doing contributions around
Istio, Envoy, Kubernetes,

00:39:01.930 --> 00:39:04.030
and some other projects
associated to that.

00:39:04.030 --> 00:39:06.340
Because this is kind of a
true community effort that

00:39:06.340 --> 00:39:10.010
has the federation elements of
multiple cloud work together,

00:39:10.010 --> 00:39:11.883
it has to be built out
of common standards.

00:39:11.883 --> 00:39:13.300
And the common
standards right now

00:39:13.300 --> 00:39:15.640
are being built out of
open source frameworks.

00:39:15.640 --> 00:39:18.290
The [INAUDIBLE] is this
shared vision of saying,

00:39:18.290 --> 00:39:20.690
this is not about what's right.

00:39:20.690 --> 00:39:21.550
Is it public cloud?

00:39:21.550 --> 00:39:22.510
Is it private cloud?

00:39:22.510 --> 00:39:24.580
Is it something else?

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:26.090
This phase is gone.

00:39:26.090 --> 00:39:28.440
It's not about where
things should go,

00:39:28.440 --> 00:39:30.190
but it's how they
should connect together,

00:39:30.190 --> 00:39:32.523
how they should be operated
together, how they be secure

00:39:32.523 --> 00:39:33.070
together.

00:39:33.070 --> 00:39:36.130
Because the whole thing is
about options, alternatives,

00:39:36.130 --> 00:39:37.360
and capabilities.

00:39:37.360 --> 00:39:40.570
And enabling essentially the
right environment for the right

00:39:40.570 --> 00:39:41.780
use case.

00:39:41.780 --> 00:39:43.030
And the last sentence is this.

00:39:43.030 --> 00:39:44.822
It's always keeping
the enterprise focused,

00:39:44.822 --> 00:39:47.290
because this is not about
creating quick prototypes,

00:39:47.290 --> 00:39:50.830
or making things run
in a small environment,

00:39:50.830 --> 00:39:54.100
but is essentially how to grow
these technologies in order

00:39:54.100 --> 00:39:57.460
to make them production
ready for enterprises.

00:39:57.460 --> 00:40:00.280
With this I want to
thank all of you.

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:03.930
[MUSIC PLAYING]

